        "#### ¿Por qué `.squeeze(-1)`?\n",
        "\n",
        "La salida de la capa final antes del `squeeze` es shape `(batch, 1)`. En JAX, es convención que funciones de perdida escalar (como binary cross-entropy) reciben vectores 1D `(batch,)` para compatibilidad con operaciones de reducción.\n",
        "\n",
        "Comparacion de shapes a lo largo del forward pass con entrada `X_tr_j` de shape `(480, 2)`:\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "Entrada x:                  (480, 2)\n",
        "Despues de capa 1 + ReLU:  (480, 32)\n",
        "Despues de capa 2 + ReLU:  (480, 32)\n",
        "Despues de capa 3:         (480, 1)  ← logit antes de sigmoid\n",
        "Despues de sigmoid:        (480, 1)\n",
        "Despues de squeeze(-1):    (480,)    ← vector 1D de probabilidades\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Loss function — binary cross-entropy"
      ],
      "id": "9e3956f5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| code-fold: true\n",
        "\n",
        "def bce_loss_jax(params, x, y):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Binary cross-entropy loss.\n",
        "\n",
        "    L = -E[ y*log(yhat) + (1-y)*log(1-yhat) ]\n",
        "\n",
        "    donde yhat es la probabilidad predicha (0 a 1).\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    # Forward pass: obtener predicciones\n",
        "    yhat = forward_jax(params, x)  # Shape: (batch,)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Clip para evitar log(0) — log(0) no está definido numericamente\n",
        "    eps = 1e-7\n",
        "    yhat = jnp.clip(yhat, eps, 1 - eps)  # yhat in [eps, 1-eps]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # BCE formula aplicada elemento a elemento\n",
        "    loss = -(y * jnp.log(yhat) + (1 - y) * jnp.log(1 - yhat))\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Retornar promedio sobre el lote\n",
        "    return jnp.mean(loss)"
